    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "60785dfac9d3a20072fd2a6a",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/98279ea765967dc3a147a8c2fba9cf6b?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGJ-6.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/98279ea765967dc3a147a8c2fba9cf6b?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGJ-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/98279ea765967dc3a147a8c2fba9cf6b?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGJ-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/98279ea765967dc3a147a8c2fba9cf6b?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGJ-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Greg Jansen",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785dfac9d3a20072fd2a6a",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "This script does not seem to be updated for XACML 2.0 in release 3.6.2. It was unable to recognize my Policy element until I changed the schema back to XACML 1.0. I think we do still need this script. It is easy to deploy a broken policy and render the repository unresponsive. Backing out policies for troubleshooting requires several steps, including turning off authorization.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Looks like updating the script only involves changing a 1 to a 2 in env-server.sh or env-server.bat.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
